= Solution
{parent=a}

The potential is smooth everywhere, so its mixed <partial derivatives> commute. The <curl of a gradient> therefore vanishes:
$$
\boxed{\nabla\times\mathbf F=\nabla\times\nabla\phi=\mathbf0}.
$$

= b
{parent=6}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The <fundamental theorem for line integrals> evaluates this <conservative vector field> integral by the change in potential. At the initial point $\phi=0$. At the final point $z=0$, so the exponential factor is one, and
$$
\boxed{\int_C\mathbf F\cdot d\mathbf r
=\phi(C_{\rm end})-\phi(C_{\rm start})
=\sin\frac\pi8\cos\frac\pi4
=\frac{\sqrt2}{2}\sin\frac\pi8}.
$$
The detailed shape of the path does not affect this <line integral>.

