Use the double-angle identity $2\sin x\cos x=\sin2x$. The <Fourier series> is already a finite trigonometric sum:
$$
\boxed{f(x)=\sin x+\sin2x+\sin3x}.
$$
In the usual <Fourier sine series> convention, $b_1=b_2=b_3=1$, all other $b_n$ vanish, and all <cosine> coefficients and the constant coefficient vanish.

= b
{parent=7}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Differentiation of the finite sum involves no convergence issue. The <derivative> has the <Fourier cosine series>
$$
\boxed{f'(x)=\cos x+2\cos2x+3\cos3x}.
$$

