= Solution
{parent=a}

In a multivariable <Taylor series>, order means total degree. The only nonzero <monomial> of total degree at most three is $xy$; there are no constant, linear, or cubic terms. Thus
$$
\boxed{\phi(x,y)=xy+O\left((x^2+y^2)^2\right)}
$$
near the origin.

= b
{parent=10}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The <gradient> vanishes at the origin. Its <Hessian matrix> there is
$$
H=\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix},
$$
with <eigenvalues> $1$ and $-1$. The quadratic term is therefore indefinite, so the origin is a **<saddle point of a scalar function>**. Equivalently, the leading term $xy$ is positive along $y=x$ and negative along $y=-x$.

